/-
# Infinite simple locally finite groups of finite rank (Kourovka Notebook Problem 1.23)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 1.23 (M. I. Kargapolov): does there exist an
infinite simple locally finite group of finite rank?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.Data.Finset.Card
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Subgroup.Simple
public import WantedExt.GroupTheory.GroupClassesShared

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.LocallyFiniteSimpleFiniteRankKourovka1Problem23Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 1.23 (M. I.
Kargapolov). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700018 (`KOU-1.23`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

Rank is the special (Mal'cev) rank: `G` has finite rank if for some `r` every finitely generated
subgroup is generated by at most `r` elements. Locally finite means every finitely generated
subgroup is finite (`IsLocallyFinite` of `GroupClassesShared`). Infinitude is required, since
finite simple groups qualify otherwise.
-/

open MathlibExt.GroupTheory.GroupClassesShared (IsLocallyFinite)

/-- `G` has finite (special) rank: for some `r`, every finitely generated subgroup of `G` is
generated by at most `r` elements. -/
def HasFiniteRank (G : Type) [Group G] : Prop :=
  ∃ r : ℕ, ∀ s : Finset G, ∃ t : Finset G, t.card ≤ r ∧
    Subgroup.closure (t : Set G) = Subgroup.closure (s : Set G)

/-- Kourovka 1.23 (M. I. Kargapolov): there is an infinite simple locally finite group of finite
rank. -/
def existsInfiniteSimpleLocallyFiniteFiniteRank : Prop :=
  ∃ (G : Type) (_ : Group G), Infinite G ∧ IsSimpleGroup G ∧ IsLocallyFinite G ∧ HasFiniteRank G

/--
Resolved false: the Kourovka Archive answers 1.23 "No", citing Shunkov: no infinite simple locally
finite group has finite rank. Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in
Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved
Problems, Problem 1.23 (M. I. Kargapolov); resolution: V. P. Shunkov, Algebra and Logic 10 (1971),
127-142, Kourovka Archive, Problem 1.23 (No).
-/
public theorem_wanted existsInfiniteSimpleLocallyFiniteFiniteRank_refuted :
    ¬ existsInfiniteSimpleLocallyFiniteFiniteRank

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.LocallyFiniteSimpleFiniteRankKourovka1Problem23Wanted
